kind:"doc",opens:"about"},{label:"Denver, Boulder, Estes Park_2026",kind:"doc",opens:"denver"},{label:"El Paso, Van Horn, Marfa, Big Bend_2025",kind:"doc",opens:"el-paso"},{label:"Arcadia, Maine_2026",kind:"doc",opens:"arcadia"},{label:"Resume",kind:"pdf",href:"/resume.pdf",download:"Chengcheng-Hou-Resume.pdf"}],j=[{id:"denver",title:"Denver, Boulder, Estes Park_2026",location:"Gore Range Overlook, Rocky Mountain National Park",statement:["Here, among stone and water and wind-shaped silence, we learn how to be with everything; faintly, we can hear a couple arguing by the lake (possibly about the emergence of an accused love affair) but their voices blur into the air as our eyes remain fixed on the mountain — to stand at the lake's edge, to drift — and to know that nothing needs to last for it to be. No attachment, love is something too complicated to comprehend at this moment."],photos:["/trips/denver/01-dscf8979.jpg","/trips/denver/02-dscf8905.jpg","/trips/denver/03-dscf9037.jpg","/trips/denver/04-dscf8915.jpg","/trips/denver/05-dscf8796.jpg","/trips/denver/06-dscf8627.jpg","/trips/denver/07-dscf8800.jpg","/trips/denver/08-dscf8670.jpg","/trips/denver/09-dscf8654.jpg","/trips/denver/10-dscf8639.jpg","/trips/denver/11-dscf8674.jpg","/trips/denver/12-dscf8533.jpg","/trips/denver/13-dscf8506.jpg","/trips/denver/14-dscf8548.jpg"]},{id:"el-paso",title:"El Paso, Van Horn, Marfa, Big Bend_2025",location:"Panther Junction Visitor Center, Big Bend",statement:["Shot with Fuji Film X100VI (with the help of their WCL lens attachment).","A visual meditation on landscape, transience, and the liminality of borders, this series traverses the vast terrains of El Paso, Marfa, and Big Bend — regions where history, isolation, and culture intersect. Through a synthesis of natural textures, shifting light, and human traces, the work examines the quiet tension between permanence and impermanence, the built and the unbuilt, the defined and the undefined."],photos:["/trips/el-paso/01-dscf6387.jpg","/trips/el-paso/02-dscf6608.jpg","/trips/el-paso/03-dscf6581.jpg","/trips/el-paso/04-dscf6630.jpg","/trips/el-paso/05-dscf6586.jpg","/trips/el-paso/06-dscf6501.jpg","/trips/el-paso/07-dscf6655.jpg","/trips/el-paso/08-dscf6526.jpg","/trips/el-paso/09-dscf6498.jpg","/trips/el-paso/10-dscf6492.jpg","/trips/el-paso/11-dscf6007.jpg","/trips/el-paso/12-dscf5996.jpg","/trips/el-paso/13-dscf6204.jpg"]},{id:"arcadia",title:"Arcadia, Maine_2026",location:"Arcadia National Park, Maine",statement:[],photos:["/trips/arcadia/01-dscf1628.jpg","/trips/arcadia/02-dscf1613.jpg","/trips/arcadia/03-dscf1610.jpg","/trips/arcadia/04-dscf1617.jpg","/trips/arcadia/05-dscf1616.jpg","/trips/arcadia/06-dscf1611.jpg","/trips/arcadia/07-dscf1526.jpg","/trips/arcadia/08-dscf1505.jpg","/trips/arcadia/09-dscf1516.jpg","/trips/arcadia/10-dscf1522.jpg","/trips/arcadia/11-dscf1487.jpg","/trips/arcadia/12-dscf1654.jpg","/trips/arcadia/13-dscf1700.jpg"]}],k="/about-me.jpg",N="Mitchell standing on a rocky summit at Arcadia National Park",_="Photo taken at Arcadia National Park, 2026",M=[{id:"introduction",question:"“Hey Mitchell, tell us a little bit more about yourself for us!”",paragraphs:["I'm Mitchell, a product designer based in New York City. I share a studio with my cat, Mai, who tends to make an appearance in most of my meetings."]},{id:"what-i-do",question:"“So, what do you do currently?”",paragraphs:["I design digital products in healthcare — tools for the clinicians who deliver care and the patients who receive it.[1] The two audiences pull in different directions. Professionals need software that's fast, clear, and trustworthy; patients are navigating something far more personal. Designing for both at once is a discipline, and it keeps the work honest.","My practice covers the full arc: research, flows, interface, prototyping, and the language inside the product itself. I pay closest attention to the parts most people skip — empty states, edge cases, error messages, the negative number, the moment before the data loads. That's where the quality of a design reveals itself, and where you can tell whether a team did the thinking. I work closely with engineers and product partners; I've come to believe that much of design is simply communicating well with the people building alongside you."],footnote:{text:"Death by a thousand clicks, by Fred Schulte and Erika Fry, Fortune March 18, 2019,",url:"https://kffhealthnews.org/health-industry/death-by-a-thousand-clicks/"}},{id:"life-outside",question:"“What do you do outside of work?”",paragraphs:["Away from the screen, I'm usually playing guitar, out walking, or photographing national parks. I'm working toward visiting all of them — roughly two a year, for now, with every intention of picking up the pace."]},{id:"my-passion",question:"“What drives you for what you do?”",paragraphs:["I care about empathy as a method, not a sentiment — for users, for teammates, for whoever sits on the other side of a decision. As the world grows louder and more automated, the value of genuinely human interaction only rises. My aim, in healthcare and beyond, is to build products that bring people closer together.","If there's something you'd like to make together, my inbox is open."]}],A=[{label:"Email",href:"mailto:design@chengchenghou.com"},{label:"Instagram",href:"https://www.instagram.com/mitchellhouu"},{label:"LinkedIn",href:"https://www.linkedin.com/in/chengcheng-hou-277225175/"},{label:"Github",href:"https://github.com/ChengchengHou"},{label:"Medium",href:"https://medium.com/@mitchellhou134s"}];function E({className:e}){return(0,t.jsxs)("div",{className:h("min-w-0 items-center gap-3",e),children:[(0,t.jsxs)("span",{className:"relative flex size-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center overflow-hidden rounded-full border-[0.75px] border-black/[0.08] bg-bg-tertiary text-sm font-semibold text-text-quaternary dark:border-white/10",children:["OR",(0,t.jsx)("img",{src:"/avatar.jpg",alt:"Chengcheng (Mitchell) Hou",className: